cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite it as below."
title: "LLM aftershock-forecast benchmark: calibration of large language model forecasts against USGS operational aftershock forecasts"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Newton
    given-names: Tyler
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-22"
abstract: >-
  A preregistered benchmark that gives language models the information the USGS operational
  aftershock forecast had at each issue time and scores their aftershock-count forecasts with
  proper scoring rules against what happened and against the official forecast, on sequences
  after the models' training cutoffs. Includes frozen scoring code, all model outputs, an
  extended exploratory set, adapted open models and live forecasts hashed before their windows.
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/tjnewton/llm-aftershock-forecast"
keywords:
  - aftershock forecasting
  - large language models
  - calibration
  - benchmark
  - seismology
  - contamination
references:
  - type: data
    title: "ANSS Comprehensive Earthquake Catalog (ComCat)"
    authors:
      - name: "U.S. Geological Survey, Earthquake Hazards Program"
    url: "https://earthquake.usgs.gov/data/comcat/"
